WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.269
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.569 --> 00:00:09.037
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.337 --> 00:00:15.449
Unit thirty-three: Be Going To (plans). Today you will talk about plans for the future.

4
00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:18.459
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.633
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.483 --> 00:00:24.531
Going to.

7
00:00:25.517 --> 00:00:27.911
Going to means used to talk about plans.

8
00:00:28.517 --> 00:00:29.889
I am going to study.

9
00:00:30.483 --> 00:00:33.089
Your turn. Say: Going to.

10
00:00:35.933 --> 00:00:36.969
Going to.

11
00:00:37.717 --> 00:00:38.625
Tomorrow.

12
00:00:39.617 --> 00:00:41.709
Tomorrow means the day after today.

13
00:00:42.317 --> 00:00:43.875
I am going to rest tomorrow.

14
00:00:44.483 --> 00:00:46.729
Your turn. Say: Tomorrow.

15
00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:50.440
Tomorrow.

16
00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:52.277
Next week.

17
00:00:53.283 --> 00:00:55.562
Next week means the week after this one.

18
00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:58.068
We are going to travel next week.

19
00:00:58.683 --> 00:01:01.301
Your turn. Say: Next week.

20
00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:05.214
Next week.

21
00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:06.707
Plan.

22
00:01:07.717 --> 00:01:09.879
Plan means an idea of what you will do.

23
00:01:10.483 --> 00:01:12.077
My plan is to study.

24
00:01:12.683 --> 00:01:14.639
Your turn. Say: Plan.

25
00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:18.339
Plan.

26
00:01:19.083 --> 00:01:20.201
I'm going to.

27
00:01:21.217 --> 00:01:23.123
I'm going to means I am going to.

28
00:01:23.717 --> 00:01:25.171
I'm going to cook dinner.

29
00:01:25.783 --> 00:01:28.761
Your turn. Say: I'm going to.

30
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:33.077
I'm going to.

31
00:01:33.817 --> 00:01:35.073
She's going to.

32
00:01:36.083 --> 00:01:38.222
She's going to means she is going to.

33
00:01:38.817 --> 00:01:40.468
She's going to visit us.

34
00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:44.142
Your turn. Say: She's going to.

35
00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.152
She's going to.

36
00:01:48.917 --> 00:01:50.231
Not going to.

37
00:01:51.217 --> 00:01:53.750
Not going to means the negative of going to.

38
00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:55.874
I'm not going to be late.

39
00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:59.623
Your turn. Say: Not going to.

40
00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:03.839
Not going to.

41
00:02:04.583 --> 00:02:05.236
Soon.

42
00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.203
Soon means in a short time from now.

43
00:02:08.817 --> 00:02:10.433
The class begins soon.

44
00:02:11.017 --> 00:02:13.495
Your turn. Say: Soon.

45
00:02:16.333 --> 00:02:17.300
Soon.

46
00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:21.971
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.817 --> 00:02:24.921
Visal, what are you going to do tomorrow?

48
00:02:26.017 --> 00:02:35.629
I am going to visit my grandmother. We use am, is or are + going to + base verb for plans. She is going to cook. They are going to travel.

49
00:02:36.717 --> 00:02:38.856
How do we make negatives and questions?

50
00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:49.866
Negative: I am not going to be late. Question: Are you going to come? What are you going to do? We answer: Yes, I am. No, I'm not.

51
00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:52.485
Which time words go with it?

52
00:02:53.583 --> 00:03:03.135
Tomorrow, next week, soon and this weekend. In speech it sounds like gonna, but we write going to. It shows what we already decided.

53
00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.858
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:06.717 --> 00:03:09.970
Grammar focus: Be going to plus base verb.

55
00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:11.399
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:12.083 --> 00:03:14.582
I am going to visit my grandmother tomorrow.

57
00:03:15.483 --> 00:03:17.216
She is going to study next week.

58
00:03:18.117 --> 00:03:19.780
They are not going to play today.

59
00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:28.323
Use am / is / are + going to + base verb for plans. Negative: am / is / are not going to. Question: Are you going to…?

60
00:03:29.083 --> 00:03:32.641
Be careful! Don't say: I going to travel soon.

61
00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:37.157
Say: I am going to travel soon.

62
00:03:37.457 --> 00:03:39.549
Add am, is or are before going to.

63
00:03:40.333 --> 00:03:43.171
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:43.967 --> 00:03:45.107
Our Plans.

65
00:03:45.407 --> 00:03:47.755
Tomorrow I am going to visit my grandmother.

66
00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:51.405
My sister is going to study for a test next week.

67
00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.643
We are going to travel to Siem Reap soon.

68
00:03:55.633 --> 00:03:58.190
My parents are not going to work on Saturday.

69
00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:00.909
What are you going to do this weekend?

70
00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.944
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:06.783 --> 00:04:08.458
I blank going to cook dinner.

72
00:04:08.758 --> 00:04:11.482
A, am. B, is. C, are.

73
00:04:15.033 --> 00:04:16.487
The answer is A: am.

74
00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:19.487
She is going to blank tomorrow.

75
00:04:19.787 --> 00:04:23.487
A, studies. B, study. C, studying.

76
00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.917
The answer is B: study.

77
00:04:30.083 --> 00:04:31.909
They blank not going to play.

78
00:04:32.209 --> 00:04:35.212
A, is. B, am. C, are.

79
00:04:38.767 --> 00:04:40.731
The answer is C: are.

80
00:04:41.883 --> 00:04:43.604
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:43.904 --> 00:04:48.765
A, I going to travel.. B, I am going to travel.. C, I am go to travel..

82
00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.601
The answer is B: I am going to travel..

83
00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:58.539
According to the reading, where are they going to travel?

84
00:04:58.839 --> 00:05:02.922
A, Siem Reap. B, Phnom Penh. C, Battambang.

85
00:05:06.467 --> 00:05:08.582
The answer is A: Siem Reap.

86
00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:13.359
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:14.217 --> 00:05:15.880
What are you going to do this weekend?

88
00:05:24.683 --> 00:05:26.160
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:40.716
This weekend I am going to visit my cousin, and we are going to play football. On Sunday I am going to help my mother cook lunch. I am not going to watch TV all day. I use going to for my plans.

90
00:05:41.016 --> 00:05:42.714
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:43.617 --> 00:05:48.161
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and be going to plus base verb.

92
00:05:48.461 --> 00:05:53.482
Today's value is planning ahead. Make a plan and take small steps every day.

93
00:05:53.782 --> 00:05:56.307
See you in Unit thirty-four. Goodbye!

94
00:05:56.607 --> 00:06:00.002
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

